.TH FILEDIFFADVANCED 1 "April 2026" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filediffadvanced \- compare files for textual and binary differences with performance metrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filediffadvanced
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filediffadvanced
compares two files for textual or binary differences using memory-mapped I/O
(mmap) for high-speed access. It supports unified diff output, side-by-side
display, multithreaded binary comparison using pthreads, and detailed
performance metrics including wall time, CPU time, and throughput.
.PP
If neither \fB\-t\fR nor \fB\-b\fR is specified, the program auto-detects
the file type by scanning for NUL bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text
Force text comparison mode (line-by-line diff using LCS algorithm).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binary
Force binary comparison mode (byte-by-byte with hex offset reporting).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unified
Unified diff output format (default for text mode).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-side\-by\-side
Side-by-side diff output format.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-brief
Only report whether files differ, without showing details.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-parallel
Enable multithreaded binary comparison using pthreads.
.TP
.BR \-j " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-threads= \fIN\fR
Number of threads for parallel mode (default: 4, max: 64).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-metrics
Print performance metrics (wall time, CPU time, throughput, memory) to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIFILE\fR ", " \-\-output= \fIFILE\fR
Write diff output to FILE instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-context= \fIN\fR
Number of context lines around changes in unified diff (default: 3).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print additional information such as file sizes and detected mode.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Files are identical.
.TP
.B 1
Files differ.
.TP
.B 2
An error occurred.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
Gracefully interrupts the comparison and exits.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
When received during a binary comparison, prints current progress to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compare two text files with unified diff:
.nf
    filediffadvanced -t -m file1.txt file2.txt
.fi
.PP
Compare binary files using 8 threads with metrics:
.nf
    filediffadvanced -b -p -j 8 --metrics big1.bin big2.bin
.fi
.PP
Side-by-side text comparison:
.nf
    filediffadvanced -y old.c new.c
.fi
.PP
Quick check if files differ:
.nf
    filediffadvanced -q a.dat b.dat
.fi
.SH SYSTEM CALLS
This program uses the following system calls:
mmap(2), munmap(2), madvise(2), open(2), close(2), fstat(2),
sigaction(2), clock_gettime(2), getrusage(2), pthread_create(3),
pthread_join(3), pthread_mutex_lock(3), getopt_long(3).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diff (1),
.BR cmp (1),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR pthreads (7)
